## Overview

Arachne is one of the six playable factions in Marathon.{{cite:techradar-launch}} GamesRadar characterises Arachne as an enigmatic, death-tinged cult whose aesthetic and goals emphasise violent conflict and its consequences.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The outlet also notes that Arachne’s design in-game is oriented around player-versus-player activity.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The faction’s representative agent is called Charter and is presented as encouraging Runners to eliminate rival players.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## What Arachne offers Runners

Runners increase their standing with Arachne by completing that faction’s contracts.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} GamesRadar lists rank-up rewards tied to Arachne that include non-chip weapon modifications and faction salvage items and weapons.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The same coverage states Arachne’s Armory inventory comprises weapons, modifications, and implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} During Marathon’s open Server Slam preview event, players were able to advance through the early Arachne faction levels and unlock portions of its progression tree.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} Bungie’s Season 2 notes also indicate that exfiltrating with Tag Chips is a way to gain Arachne reputation.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

## Recent changes and tuning

Patch 1.0.0.4 (March 11, 2026) raised the amount of starting ammunition included in Arachne’s complimentary Sponsored Kits.{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}} Season 2 reworked Priority Contracts to prioritise loot rewards and removed faction-reputation requirements from those contracts.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Bungie also introduced new Season 2 implant and chip content along with additional tuning as part of the season update.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} In Ranked mode, Tag Chips appear as loot that automatically sells when exfiltrated and contributes to a team’s score.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

