## Setting

Cryo Archive occupies the Marathon ship’s first playable deck, a derelict section of the UESC Marathon that drifts in orbit and houses arrays of cryogenic pods, medical facilities, and storage wings used during the colony’s voyage.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The deck is presented in‑game as a preserved section of the ship that contains valuable goods and information for crews willing to brave its hazards.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Layout and features

The playable area on Cryo Archive is formed from six linked wings arranged around a central hub, requiring traversal between wings and the hub during runs.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Scattered through the deck are seven heavily defended Vaults; each Vault has its own entry requirements and needs a particular Vault Key to open.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Level design alternates narrow approaches with very large chambers intended to force opposing crews and ship defenses into conflict as teams attempt to unlock Vaults.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} 

## Access rules and progression

Queueing for Cryo Archive requires a minimum Runner Level of 25, progression through all six factions, and a Loadout Value of at least 5,000 credits.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Runs build a temporary Security Clearance metric by interacting with ship systems and surviving long enough to use higher‑tier systems; access to doors, supply rooms, and exfil points is gated by that clearance.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Vault Keys appear in multiple places: planet‑side activities, on the ship during runs, and as loot taken from defeated enemy Runner crews.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} While Cryo Archive is active, CyberAcme supplies a pool of seven Cryo contracts; completing a contract removes it from that week’s pool.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Each finished Cryo contract awards a random high‑rarity item, and progress toward Cryo Archive Codex rewards carries over between weekly appearances.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} 

## Notable changes and schedule

Cryo Archive first opened for play on the weekend beginning Friday, March 20.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Season 2 adjusted Cryo contract progression so some objectives can be advanced across multiple runs and retained the seventh contract’s connection to the Compiler.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The Nightfall Refresh later altered the recurrence window so Cryo Archive ran weekly from Thursdays through Mondays beginning October 15.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Vault Breaker, a roguelite experimental PvE mode set inside Cryo Archive, was introduced in mid‑Season 2 as a limited event and later returned in subsequent windows.{{cite:bungie-press-mid-season-2}}{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}} A November 10 patch fixed an issue in Cryo Archive’s Vault 4 that could cause players to become stuck.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}} Update 1.1.9.2 also changed Armory offerings tied to Vault Breaker and limited availability of certain Vault Keys and Armory items during the event window.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

