## Surface Zones

Marathon presents three planet-side maps that players can encounter on Tau Ceti IV: Perimeter, Dire Marsh, and Outpost.{{cite:bungie-vidoc}}

## Perimeter and Dire Marsh

Perimeter is located on the colony’s outer edge and is positioned as the most approachable map for new players.{{cite:gamesradar-maps}} Dire Marsh is built around a disaster site with a central complex and emphasizes direct, combat-heavy encounters.{{cite:gamesradar-maps}} Both Perimeter and Dire Marsh were available to play during the Marathon Server Slam event.{{cite:gamesradar-maps}}

## Outpost

Outpost represents a UESC military facility organized around a tall vertical structure known as the Pinwheel.{{cite:gamesradar-maps}} According to the developers, the map becomes available a day after launch and requires players to reach Runner Level 12 to enter.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Outpost also presents intermittent environmental hazards called Heat Cascades and uses security-card gated areas; obtaining cards is required to reach the Pinwheel’s interior, which contains high‑value rewards.{{cite:pcgamer-review}}

## Cryo Archive (End‑Game)

Cryo Archive is the end‑game location aboard the derelict UESC Marathon and combines vault puzzles with multilayered mechanics.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} Access to the ship requires players to satisfy multiple conditions: attain at least Runner Level 25, finish liaison contracts for every faction so all six are unlocked, and equip a loadout valued at 5,000 credits or more.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} Players who meet these criteria may claim a single Sponsored Kit from the Armory designed to support initial Cryo Archive attempts.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}} The activity is tuned for three-player crews and opens on weekends, with an initial availability window beginning March 20 as announced by Bungie.{{cite:bungie-cryo-archive}}

## Unlocking Zones and Expedition Access

Seasonal progression increases the game’s power floor and gates higher-difficulty content such as Cryo Archive behind earned progression.{{cite:bungie-introducing-seasons}} In Expedition mode (Phase 1), players can run Perimeter, Night Marsh, Outpost, or Cryo Archive as long as those zones have been unlocked via Runner Level.{{cite:bungie-expedition-phase-1}} For Season 2, if a player had unlocked and completed Dire Marsh in the previous season they begin with both the day and Night variants of the Marsh available; otherwise, the Marsh maps unlock when the player reaches Runner Level 3.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

