## Overview

NuCaloric is presented as an agricultural company and Marathon faction whose stated mission is to supply food and help humanity endure in the colony setting.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The faction was among the early groups players could access during Marathon’s Server Slam preview event.{{cite:bungie-server-slam}} A NuCaloric contract was added to the game in an early post-launch patch (Update 1.0.0.4, March 11, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-0-0-4}}

## What NuCaloric offers Runners

Ranking up with NuCaloric grants consumable items, faction-branded salvage, and implant rewards.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} The NuCaloric armory stocks healing consumables that can cure negative conditions, consumables that revive the user, protective shield items, and various implants.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}} Bungie also published a suite of head, torso, and leg implants tied to NuCaloric that emphasize restorative and survivability functions.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} GamesRadar documents ways to earn NuCaloric reputation, such as completing the faction’s contracts, opening Medical Cabinets, harvesting plant salvage, and exfiltrating with NuCaloric valuables.{{cite:gamesradar-factions}}

## Recent changes and events

The Nightfall Refresh introduced a NuCaloric Reward Pass that is provided at no extra charge to Marathon owners (Update 1.1.9.2, October 6, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}} Bungie described the same update as including a NuCaloric-themed set of Reward Pass skins.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} Nightfall Refresh also performed a progression wipe that reset Runner, Cradle, and Faction levels as part of its release.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}} A later patch corrected an issue where Stickers applied to NuCal weapon styles were not rendering properly (Update 1.1.9.7, November 10, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-7}} An earlier fix addressed an incorrect icon for the NuCaloric Armored Barter in the Armory (Update 1.1.0.1, June 9, 2026).{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-0-1}}

