## Overview

Ranked evaluates looting efficiency, player-versus-player outcomes, and calculated risk across score-based runs.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Entry and Holotags

Entering a Ranked run requires a Holotag, which determines both the run’s score target and the penalty applied for failing to exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Holotags remain in a player’s possession after a successful exfil and may be sold for their full credit value following exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} The Armory sells Holotags up to the tier a player has unlocked via their current rank.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} In Season 2, queuing requires bringing a Holotag that matches the player’s current rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Bronze Holotags impose a 3,000 score target and a 600 loss penalty.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Silver Holotags set a 5,000 score target and a 2,000 loss penalty.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Gold Holotags set a 7,000 score target and a 4,200 loss penalty.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Platinum Holotags set a 10,000 score target and an 8,000 loss penalty.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Diamond Holotags set a 15,000 score target and a 15,000 loss penalty.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Pinnacle Holotags set a 20,000 score target and a 20,000 loss penalty.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Scoring and Ranked Points

A team’s combined Holotag credit value establishes the score target for that run.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Items in a player’s starting loadout are excluded from the score calculation.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Teams must exfil with at least the score target to receive Ranked Points; exfiltrating below the target yields no change to RP.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} The loss penalty applied when a team fails to exfil is determined by the team’s combined Holotag value, and RP is deducted only on failed exfils.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Tag Chips contribute as loot toward the score target, provide capacity for overperformance, and are automatically sold on exfil.{{cite:bungie-ranked}}

## Ranks and Season 2 changes

Players progress through six rank categories (Bronze up to Pinnacle), with each category divided into three tiers.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Ranked first ran in a beta weekend from March 21–24, 2026 during Season 1.{{cite:bungie-ranked}} Season 2 brought Ranked back on June 14 with changes to rewards and progression.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Season 2 merged the previous Low and High Stakes queues into a single queue and introduced a minimum 5,000 Loadout value for entry.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} The season also sped up progression and altered how win/loss point adjustments are calculated based on average match rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}} Additionally, Season 2 introduced a daily Ranked Sponsored Kit containing a loadout scaled to a player’s rank.{{cite:bungie-welcome-season-2}}

