## Overview

Recon is the Runner shell built around information-gathering and tracking duties.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} It is intended to spot hostile actors and follow their movement patterns.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}} The shell's toolkit includes an ability that sends out scanning pulses, a deployable tracking drone, and visualized traces of enemy footsteps.{{cite:bungie-runner-shells}}

## Abilities

Recon's Prime ability is Echo Pulse.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} The Tactical ability for Recon is Tracker Drone.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} As of Update 1.1.9.2 (October 6, 2026), Echo Pulse emits its scans forward in the direction the player aims rather than radiating in all directions.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}} The same update also causes Echo Pulse to briefly stagger non-Runner hostile combatants and to block their combat abilities the first time they are hit.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

## Traits

Recon possesses the Interrogation trait.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} It also includes the Stalker Protocol trait.{{cite:pcgamer-guide}} Update 1.1.9.2 introduced a two-second delay before pinged Recon players receive the Interrogation notification.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

## Notable Changes

Bungie described the Echo Pulse adjustments in the Nightfall Refresh as intended to reduce how dominant the ability feels and to make it less mandatory in encounters.{{cite:bungie-nightfall-refresh}} In the Update 1.1.9.2 patch notes, developers explained that narrowing the scan area to a forward cone was chosen to force Recon users to anticipate enemy locations in three dimensions.{{cite:bungie-update-1-1-9-2}}

